Package: ModalLasso
Type: Package
Title: Penalized Parametric Modal Regression for High-Dimensional Positive Responses
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Christian", "Galarza", email = "chedgala@espol.edu.ec", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Victor H.", "Lachos", email = "hlachos@uconn.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Variable selection and estimation for parametric modal regression
    with continuous positive responses (Gamma, Weibull and Lognormal families)
    under L1 (Lasso), elastic-net and adaptive-Lasso penalties. The conditional
    mode is linked to a linear predictor through a logarithmic link using the
    mode reparameterization of Galarza and Lachos (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2603.07099>. The penalized log-likelihood is maximized
    with a proximal Newton algorithm (iteratively reweighted penalized least
    squares): at each iteration the modal log-likelihood is replaced by a local
    quadratic surrogate in the linear predictor, which yields a pseudo-response
    and a working weight in closed form, and the resulting weighted penalized
    least-squares subproblem is solved by the coordinate-descent solver of
    'glmnet'. The regularization parameter is chosen along a warm-started path by
    the extended Bayesian information criterion (EBIC).
